// endpoint_find_pull_request_owner.proto — FindPullRequestOwner: which
// workspace owns the pull request a clicked link names. WEB LINK section.
//
// A SHIFT-CLICK ON A PULL REQUEST LINK SWITCHES TO ITS WORKSPACE. A page asks
// this for the link's url and, given an owner, makes the feed's one jump to it
// (`SelectInEditor`, after `OpenWorkspace` for a closed owner), rather than
// opening the link in the browser. The daemon alone decides whether a url
// names a pull request and who owns it, so the page never parses a GitHub
// address of its own.
//
// THE OWNER IS THE CANONICAL OWNED LINK'S WORKSPACE: the workspace that stored
// the pull request's link owned (agentrepl.v1.WorkspaceLinkOwned). Among open
// workspaces that is the one holding the pull request's owned-link
// subscription, which the store admits for one workspace only, so at most one
// open workspace is ever the answer. A closed workspace's ownership ends with
// its close, yet its owned link stays stored: when no open workspace owns the
// pull request, the most recently closed workspace that stored it owned is the
// owner, so a merged pull request still reaches the workspace that made it.

